  "summary": "Princess Märtha Louise of Norway, the 52-year-old daughter of King Harald V and Queen Sonja and fourth in line to the Norwegian throne, married American self-proclaimed shaman Durek Verrett in an unconventional yet formally sanctioned Church of Norway ceremony. The wedding took place on Saturday afternoon at the four-star Hotel Union in Geiranger—a picturesque village nestled beneath the Geiranger fjord—drawing onlookers despite overcast weather. Märtha Louise, who divorced Norwegian author Ari Behn in 2017, was accompanied by seven bridesmaids, including her teenage daughters Leah and Emma Behn. The 350-guest event included prominent European royals: Crown Prince Haakon and Crown Princess Mette-Marit of Norway; Crown Princess Victoria and Prince Daniel of Sweden; and Prince Constantijn and Princess Laurentien of the Netherlands. Known for her longstanding interest in spirituality, Märtha Louise has identified as a clairvoyant and operated a healing school focused on angelic communication for a decade. In 2022, she officially stepped back from royal duties to prioritize her entrepreneurial work with Verrett and to draw a clearer boundary between their private ventures and the Norwegian royal institution. Verrett, who brands himself on social media as a 'servant of God' and 'energy activator', counts Gwyneth Paltrow—whom he refers to as his 'soul sister'—among his high-profile clients."
}
```

